<item><title>Malabo faces food inflation and power cuts as year-end demand rises</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gq/malabo-faces-food-inflation-and-power-cuts-as-year-end-ca5f46/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gq/malabo-faces-food-inflation-and-power-cuts-as-year-end-ca5f46/</guid><category>Equatorial Guinea</category><description>October inflation crossed the CEMAC threshold, while outages are cutting business income and making food and seasonings more expensive.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:01:04 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gq/malabo-faces-food-inflation-and-power-cuts-as-year-end-ca5f46/share.jpg" length="44659" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gq/malabo-faces-food-inflation-and-power-cuts-as-year-end-ca5f46/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
